# Battery-swap bench, 2026-08-27 evening — does one MAVSDK process survive the
# flight controller being power-cycled? (the seam a between-flights pack swap
# relies on: the orchestrator keeps running on the CM4's powerbank while the
# FC reboots on the new pack). Probe = System() + embedded mavsdk_server on
# udpin://0.0.0.0:14540 through the same mavlink-router the mission uses.
# Props OFF, aircraft on the bench indoors (0 GPS sats, so the full
# orchestrator could not start — its _wait_for_gps is mandatory).
# Timeline (CM4 clock): 07:01 probe up · 07:08:29 pack pulled → is_connected
# False, streams stop · ~07:33:45 pack replugged · 07:33:52 is_connected True
# · armed stream ticking again 07:33:56 · battery stream 07:34:31 — same
# process, no restart, no stream ended. VERDICT: PASS.
# ("armed = False" 1 Hz ticks collapsed below; 469 in total, none lost after
# reconnect.)
